main HOLD. Empty fixture provider payload is not content qualification.\n\n--- Prior retained history (unchanged) ---\n\nCurrent engineering source refresh: ordinary merge of accepted integration `e2c81adc` into the existing branch; new source `2314aea9`, tree `2987ed3a`. The OAuth build acquisition guard and changelog selection are preserved.\n\nIndependent current LIGHT evidence: Toolkit 179 PASS, guard 41 PASS, configured static/type checks, workflow generation and a controlled real Invoke acquisition success/failure boundary passed. The controlled OAuth pair is synthetic structural evidence, not approved provider content. Local complete Runtime suite is NOT RUN for this union because TMP capacity is below its 1.2 GB admission floor. Fresh exact-source hosted CI is required; merge, authoritative OAuth acquisition, Runtime publication and RCC native qualification remain pending. Production RCC remains v18.19.3.\n\n<details><summary>Preserved prior PR description and evidence</summary>\n\nCurrent candidate `87e412f89b201c697d3e6bd4bd34031cdbd14df3`, tree `638b960a3700bbbba3026874efb158fa6e95117f`, preserves the original changelog repair through ordinary merge `0df31528` of `729594fc` and accepted integration `fbde0d3a`.\n\nThe OAuth generation task previously ignored failed GitHub acquisition and could package empty strings or API error payloads. It now checks bounded acquisition, validates both UTF-8 YAML structures before replacement, and atomically writes the generated module while preserving the previous file and primary error on failure. The existing Invoke entry point delegates to the Runtime Poetry environment for declared PyYAML; activated RCC/Poetry environment selection is verified. Source repository/authority and task interface remain unchanged. No replacement configuration, guessed provider policy or synthetic release payload is introduced.\n\nValidation: RED3→GREEN41 focused cases;1,173 package tests passed with13 existing skips; Toolkit69, complete configured lint/type335 plus explicit helper checks, and all eight workflow roundtrips passed. The exact committed Invoke→Poetry gateway was executed with outer YAML import forbidden and controlled GitHub responses. All1,404 unrelated blobs/modes and268 tracked native producer inputs remain exact. Independent source/gateway GO SHA256 `48d03bc4256c13ceb6fee1cf81e86bd56e6fd2af2903baf99444d32101693229`. Fresh hosted checks are required; guard adoption can fail closed while the approved configuration pair is unavailable. Valid structure alone does not qualify provider content, and this fix does not repair artifacts recovered from older immutable release sources.\n\nOAuth source authority, provider-content acceptance, full current CI and Runtime1.0.3 publication remain HOLD. Canonical operations guidance records acquisition/atomic generation/environment selection and dry-run/generated-content boundaries. Upstream disposition: none.\n\nRetained changelog repair and original evidence follow:\n\nThe pinned GitHub release action ignores `changelog_file` whenever `release_text` is nonempty. The native Runtime generator supplied both, so publication would bypass the dedicated changelog. Remove the override and prepare the exact H2 `actions-runtime-1.0.3` that the pinned parser selects. Keep unpublished candidate status and outstanding gates under Unreleased; existing 1.0.1/1.0.2 history remains intact.\n\nPR304 was accepted as merge `19380993febaa71238eaee3026b5c808773283ff` with all 23 checks passing. This PR now targets integration. The refreshed head `729594fc04758502ec2ed985adb428e2863a3bb1` has the identical complete tree `1db860bf248e83aeedf521044633bbd221902282` as the independently reviewed source; its normal merge adds the accepted base ancestry. This changes the generator, generated workflow, dedicated changelog, focused contract regression, and canonical operations guide. Tag admission, pinned release action, artifact upload ordering, credentials, and immutable no-overwrite safeguards are unchanged.\n\nIndependent source review GO at `bad6a44752438216c47ebab7fac520e174f9649a`, tree `1db860bf248e83aeedf521044633bbd221902282`. Worker reports regression RED before the fix, canonical generation, 97 focused release tests passed, Ruff and whitespace checks passed through RCC. Those local stdout/task files were not retained, so they are attributed results rather than independently replayable test evidence. All required workflows must pass on the refreshed head. Earlier temporary-base runs omitted the Runtime package and PyPI candidate gates; they do not replace the new integration-base checks. The static contract test does not execute upstream submark.\n\nRuntime1.0.3 remains unpublished. #134/#153 and final source/platform acceptance remain open; #211 Homebrew installation/upgrade proof follows native publication. Canvas and private Package inspection are separate graph successors. Review receipt SHA-256: `fb539283e97c35bc33835e382f41a96d6bbdcb47210f96982b404586029115a6`. Upstream disposition: none.\n\n</details>\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:39:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T01:19:27Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"eb39388640d2b7dac30b72eb584e56ffacd1b4b7","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/actions/pulls/307/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/actions/pulls/307/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/actions/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/actions/issues/307/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/actions/statuses/06086c63a681bb9cb117387675c98ca3824ce7cc","head":{"label":"joshyorko:fix/runtime-release-changelog-selection-20261010","ref":"fix/runtime-release-changelog-selection-20261010","sha":"06086c63a681bb9cb117387675c98ca3824ce7cc","user":{"login":"j